<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip II of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1556">1556</a>–<a href="/years/1598">1598</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from 1556 to 1598, ruling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> at the height of its power. After the death of the Portuguese king Sebastião at Alcácer Quibir in 1578 and the resulting succession crisis, he became King of Portugal in 1580, uniting the two crowns. His reign also saw the revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Armada</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1588.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain.jpg" alt="Philip II of Spain" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sofonisba Anguissola · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Philip_II_of_Spain_by_Sofonisba_Anguissola_-_002b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
